/*
 * SUIT manifest vectors, issue #78. LITERALS, on purpose, like vectors.h: a
 * vector computed from the code it pins moves whenever that code moves.
 *
 * Fixed inputs:
 *   key     the RFC 6979 A.2.5 P-256 test key (test/unit/test_model_p256.c);
 *           only its public half is here, as the element's slot-2 key
 *   image   64 bytes, 0x00..0x3F; size 64; sequence 7
 *   vendor  f5ce0048-68e5-5fcf-b79b-5b1cffbf22ac (include/tfw/config.h)
 *   class   dc97b9d0-38d6-58e0-bb18-98bb2414d131, the ATmega2560's
 *   component [[h'00']]
 *
 * SUIT_MANIFEST is the bstr-wrapped manifest, SUIT_TBS the COSE Sig_structure
 * go-xkms signs, SUIT_ENVELOPE the signed envelope. The signatures are ECDSA,
 * made once outside this tree; ECDSA is randomised, so they are not
 * reproducible, only verifiable -- which is all a literal needs.
 *
 * SUIT_ENVELOPE_CLASS_328P is the same image signed for the 328P's class id;
 * SUIT_ENVELOPE_UNKNOWN carries a fourth manifest member, 5: h''. Both are
 * validly signed, so a refusal of either is the profile's and not the
 * signature's.
 */
